okf_version: "1.0"
task: "User: 메시지를 주입할때마다 우리는 여러가지 옵션을 제공하고있어 하나만하고있는게 아냐. 따라서 다양한경로에서 다양한 파라메터에 맞게 주입하도록 지원하게해줘 (support injecting into Muse through the several paths with the parameters each one carries, not one fixed way)."
finding_first: "Research confirmed Muse Code exposes an external injection surface: `muse serve` hosts the Muse Session Protocol (MSP) over the client's stdio, `muse schema generate-json-schema` exports the exact wire contract of the installed binary (47 methods, error table, method index), and the official TypeScript SDK `@muse-code/sdk` 1.3.0 (npm) wraps it ('connect to a Muse Code session, drive turns, and fold the event stream'); `muse session-message list|send` is the peer bus (Windows-unsupported, and closed on this machine: external_agent_ingress_closed). TUI keystrokes are therefore one path among several, not the only one."
before: "Interactive Muse launches injected messages one way: call_with_channel_proxy with bracketed paste and fire-and-forget submit (muse_runtime_context.py:344)."
built:
  muse_msp: "ciel_runtime_support/muse_msp.py - NDJSON JSON-RPC 2.0 client for a `muse serve` host: initialize + initialized handshake, session/start, session/resume, turn/start (ifBusy queue|steer|replace, displayText, reasoningEffort, parts), turn/steer (expectedTurnId), turn/interrupt, approval/decide, userInput/answer, notification pump with wait_for/drain, UUIDv7 command ids that survive a restart per key, approval-mode alias normalization, reader/close hardening."
  muse_injection: "ciel_runtime_support/muse_injection.py - one option model (transport, intent queue|steer|replace|notify, wake idle|now|notify, display text, reasoning effort, sandbox posture flags, durability, workspace, session, provider/model/base-url, permission profile, explicit command id, timeout) mapped onto four paths (msp, console, exec, session-message) with capability reporting per path; serve/exec/session-message argv builders; config reader (muse.injection + meta provider defaults) with per-call overlay; ingress probe parsing."
  probe: "scripts/probe_muse_msp_injection.py - opens a real host (resolving the WSL muse path), starts an echo session, delivers one message per intent, prints receipts and notifications."
live_verification: "Muse Code 1.3.0-R3233.1, 2026-09-19, through our own client: initialize -> muse 1.3.0, schema fingerprint sha256:ab69549a7ebb423fce94068762da0b5ff3cdec1f8fc263dcc17248eda117f852 v1, durability ephemeral; session/start -> 01a0b82c-… (provider echo); queue -> turn/start accepted disposition=started; steer -> accepted disposition=steered (same turn id); replace -> accepted (host answered queued because the first turn had already finished); redelivery of the same key -> command id rotated, no conflict; notification session/started; host returncode 0."
protocol_facts_learned_live:
  - "The handshake is gated: before `initialized` every request answers -32600 notInitialized, and clientInfo.name must match ^[a-z0-9_]+$ (-32602 invalidParams otherwise)."
  - "Wire approval modes are allowAll|promptUnmatched|onRequest|denyUnmatched, not the CLI spellings (untrusted|on-request|never); a mode that exceeds the host's sealed startup mode is rejected with -32030."
  - "workspaceRoot must be an absolute path as the host sees it (Windows paths fail across WSL)."
  - "An applied commandId reused for a new command answers -32030 command_id_conflict, so the service rotates the id after an acknowledged delivery and reuses it only for an unacknowledged attempt."
  - "Closing stdout while the reader is parked in readline raises ValueError: PyMemoryView_FromBuffer (seen live); close() now reaps the process and joins the reader first."
tests: "tests/test_muse_injection.py - 30 tests: UUIDv7 shape/order, per-key id reuse and rotation, handshake gating and error mapping against a scripted host over real stdio, turn/start parameters per intent, turn/steer expectedTurnId, notification wait, option parsing/validation, config defaults with overlay, argv builders per path, capability rules (msp without host, exec with a live session, Windows session-message, closed ingress, notify-only refusal), service delivery receipts, command-id rotation, approval-mode aliases. unit group 1506 OK (45 skipped); ruff clean."
not_done:
  - "The launch path still runs the TUI through the console proxy; switching an interactive launch to an MSP host the runtime owns is a bigger change and was not made here."
  - "view/subscribe and view/page answered methodNotFound to the minimal client on this build, so live item streaming through our own client is unverified (the SDK documents the facade)."
  - "session-message cannot be exercised on this machine: ingress closed, and Muse documents the bus as unavailable on Windows."
state: "Working tree; committed by itself."
